WEBVTT

00:01:30.650 --> 00:01:36.380
Go, Maihama! Go, go, go!

00:01:36.890 --> 00:01:40.000
"We are such stuff as dreams are made on."

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:41.730
Who said that?

00:01:41.730 --> 00:01:43.460
Shakespeare.

00:01:43.800 --> 00:01:46.430
A midsummer night's dream, I suppose.

00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:48.700
Mizuki, can you put that in the locker?

00:01:48.700 --> 00:01:49.640
Sure thing!

00:01:55.110 --> 00:01:58.850
It's a collection of the club's productions!
C'mon, let's watch!

00:01:58.850 --> 00:02:00.150
That sounds like fun!

00:02:00.650 --> 00:02:03.820
All you guys have been
doing is goofing around!

00:02:03.820 --> 00:02:05.080
We don't have time!

00:02:06.320 --> 00:02:09.720
But the video club's room
has all kinds of neat stuff in it!

00:02:10.460 --> 00:02:12.890
I'm sorry I asked you to help me like this.

00:02:13.300 --> 00:02:16.320
There's stuff I need to get out
of here before summer break.

00:02:16.770 --> 00:02:18.630
It's a real pain, isn't it?

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:23.540
Anyway, shouldn't you hurry up and
figure out who I'll be acting with?

00:02:23.540 --> 00:02:24.840
You're right.

00:02:24.840 --> 00:02:27.810
I have to get this shot during the break.

00:02:27.810 --> 00:02:29.310
What'll I do?

00:02:29.310 --> 00:02:31.710
Well, I think Sogoru would be good for it.

00:02:31.950 --> 00:02:36.350
He's right. Why not swallow
your pride and ask him, Ryoko?

00:02:36.850 --> 00:02:38.650
Who would ask that guy for a favor?!

00:02:49.770 --> 00:02:52.560
"The Day the World Ended..."

00:03:18.340 --> 00:03:20.510
What is all this?

00:03:29.260 --> 00:03:32.190
There's something... overpowering about it.

00:03:38.600 --> 00:03:43.360
15th term... That'd make him
a senior now. Tohru Kanou...

00:03:43.970 --> 00:03:45.130
Is he a phantom club member?

00:04:02.220 --> 00:04:04.450
All right! I'm kicking ass!

00:04:06.890 --> 00:04:09.550
Seriously, I'm ready to get
the record for Japan!

00:04:10.300 --> 00:04:12.430
So, how'd I look from here?
Did you see me?

00:04:12.430 --> 00:04:14.490
Oh, sorry. I wasn't watching.

00:04:14.600 --> 00:04:18.160
Right, the record for Japan! Talk about
your reach exceeding your grasp!

00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:20.060
Check them out.

00:04:20.210 --> 00:04:25.230
You think so? Okay, since
you're here, you can time me.

00:04:25.610 --> 00:04:28.170
Look, we're not even <i>in</i> the swim club!

00:04:28.280 --> 00:04:31.080
Besides, we didn't
come here to see you!

00:04:31.850 --> 00:04:34.510
See, we're looking for someone
to play the lead in our movie!

00:04:34.790 --> 00:04:37.860
What, you guys still haven't
decided on someone to play it?

00:04:37.860 --> 00:04:40.060
And whose fault is that?!

00:04:40.060 --> 00:04:42.890
We just can't find anyone
to replace you, Sogoru!

00:04:43.700 --> 00:04:44.960
Yeah, I suppose!

00:04:44.960 --> 00:04:48.330
There's a scene where you leap
into the ocean to save the heroine!

00:04:48.330 --> 00:04:50.860
So we need someone who can swim!

00:04:51.340 --> 00:04:54.140
So, you came to ask me to do it again?

00:04:54.140 --> 00:04:57.630
Sorry, no way. No more
kissing scenes with Tomigai!

00:04:58.280 --> 00:05:02.850
That's why we're waiting around
here to ask Hayase to do it.

00:05:02.850 --> 00:05:04.180
I wish he'd hurry!

00:05:06.420 --> 00:05:07.920
Hi there. Came to watch us?

00:05:07.920 --> 00:05:10.550
Oh... Hi! Sorry to bother!

00:05:18.830 --> 00:05:21.390
Who's Shizuno-sempai taking
to the summer festival?

00:05:21.700 --> 00:05:24.040
Oh yeah, that's coming up again, soon.

00:05:24.040 --> 00:05:26.310
It's on the night of this year's
closing ceremony, right?

00:05:26.310 --> 00:05:29.830
I'll bet she's gotten a ton
of invitations already.

00:05:30.280 --> 00:05:33.800
Kaminagi and I have
always gone together.

00:05:34.550 --> 00:05:37.920
Oh... So, that's the sort
of relationship you have.

00:05:37.920 --> 00:05:40.750
Th-That was when
we were little kids, you idiot!

00:05:40.950 --> 00:05:44.660
Oh, yeah. When I started going to it with
Hayase and the guys in middle school,

00:05:44.660 --> 00:05:46.520
she swore she'd
stop going with me.

00:05:47.690 --> 00:05:49.060
What's with you?!

00:05:49.060 --> 00:05:50.820
Ushio! Lemme go, you idiot!

00:05:51.760 --> 00:05:54.030
C'mon, don't be shy. Go on!

00:05:54.430 --> 00:05:55.660
Kawaguchi...

00:05:55.970 --> 00:05:59.440
He came all the way here,
but couldn't bring himself to go in!

00:05:59.440 --> 00:06:01.940
You're wrong! I just...

00:06:01.940 --> 00:06:04.600
You just want to come back
to the swim club, right?

00:06:09.920 --> 00:06:12.350
I still won't forgive this jerk!

00:06:14.150 --> 00:06:15.520
I see.

00:06:17.260 --> 00:06:18.780
Um... Excuse me...

00:06:19.530 --> 00:06:21.960
Um... The summer festival!

00:06:23.160 --> 00:06:26.400
Could I go with you this year?
Kawaguchi can come, too.

00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:27.770
Count me in!

00:06:27.770 --> 00:06:30.030
You'll let me come too, won't you?

00:06:30.270 --> 00:06:32.700
Seriously?! All right!

00:06:32.700 --> 00:06:34.670
You <i>are</i> coming, right?

00:06:35.610 --> 00:06:36.710
I guess...

00:06:36.710 --> 00:06:38.380
Kaminagi, I've got it!

00:06:38.380 --> 00:06:41.140
Why not have Kawaguchi
play the lead in your movie?

00:06:41.380 --> 00:06:42.810
Huh? Lead?

00:06:43.050 --> 00:06:46.540
That's right! Kawaguchi would be
a perfect substitute for Sogoru!

00:06:46.690 --> 00:06:48.450
A substitute for Kyo?!

00:06:48.690 --> 00:06:49.880
Whoops! Uh-oh...

00:06:50.060 --> 00:06:51.960
Leave me OUT!

00:06:53.660 --> 00:06:54.460
Oh, well...

00:06:54.460 --> 00:06:56.060
Sorry.

00:06:56.060 --> 00:06:59.000
Forget it.
I'll see what I can do about him.

00:06:59.230 --> 00:07:03.030
What's wrong with playing the lead
in a movie? I'll do it if you want.

00:07:03.270 --> 00:07:05.070
Ushio, you're just sorta...

00:07:05.070 --> 00:07:06.940
I wonder what's keeping Hayase.

00:07:07.540 --> 00:07:10.840
Hayase said he was headed over to the
seniors' classrooms again, so he'd be late.

00:07:10.840 --> 00:07:11.780
The seniors?

00:07:11.780 --> 00:07:13.870
Yeah. He's been dating a senior lately.

00:07:19.120 --> 00:07:21.090
Isn't that Hayase,
one of the freshmen?

00:07:21.090 --> 00:07:23.020
I heard he's dating Sachi.

00:07:23.020 --> 00:07:23.960
Really?!

00:07:23.960 --> 00:07:25.760
But I've never seen them together.

00:07:25.760 --> 00:07:27.490
Yeah. Me, neither.

00:07:27.660 --> 00:07:30.290
He told me something weird's going on.

00:07:30.500 --> 00:07:34.400
They've been in the same school since April,
but he says he hasn't seen her once.

00:07:36.270 --> 00:07:36.700
That's...

00:07:36.700 --> 00:07:39.260
His girlfriend's name... Do you know it?

00:07:39.610 --> 00:07:41.770
I think it's Sachiko Tsumura.

00:07:41.770 --> 00:07:43.110
I see.

00:07:43.110 --> 00:07:44.510
You know her?

00:07:44.510 --> 00:07:45.600
No.

00:07:46.180 --> 00:07:50.380
Oh! Sempai, is there a
Tohru Kanou in your class?

00:07:51.180 --> 00:07:52.320
Why do you ask?

00:07:52.320 --> 00:07:54.290
He's apparently an
upperclassman in the video club.

00:07:54.290 --> 00:07:56.350
I was thinking of asking
him about some stuff.

00:07:57.420 --> 00:07:59.990
Kanou's been out sick.

00:07:59.990 --> 00:08:02.930
Maybe he'll be well enough
to come back next term.

00:08:03.400 --> 00:08:05.590
Oh, I see. He's sick...

00:08:11.040 --> 00:08:13.000
They're Cerebrants who died in battle?!

00:08:13.470 --> 00:08:15.940
Yes. Both Sachiko Tsumura
and Tohru Kanou.

00:08:16.010 --> 00:08:19.340
They were both comrades
who once fought with us.

00:08:19.610 --> 00:08:24.050
Our deaths are integrated into
this world in various ways.

00:08:24.050 --> 00:08:26.120
They "die in accidents"...
"Transfer to other schools"...

00:08:26.120 --> 00:08:27.920
Or are still "here," but you
never see them anymore.

00:08:27.920 --> 00:08:31.620
So, you mean... Hayase doesn't know
the girl he's waiting for is dead?!

00:08:31.960 --> 00:08:33.360
It can't be helped!

00:08:33.360 --> 00:08:37.350
It was decided in order to minimize
inconsistencies in this world.

00:08:37.600 --> 00:08:39.060
But, occasionally!

00:08:39.060 --> 00:08:41.430
Occasionally, there are those
who notice the inconsistencies.

00:08:41.530 --> 00:08:44.200
And that is when a new Cerebrant is born.

00:08:45.740 --> 00:08:49.040
I came here in order to awaken you.

00:08:49.310 --> 00:08:51.240
So, then what <i>are</i> Cerebrants?

00:08:51.240 --> 00:08:53.400
Who are we, exactly?!

00:08:53.750 --> 00:08:56.440
We are the ones who take on
the distortions of this world.

00:08:56.850 --> 00:09:01.290
The truth is, even we don't understand
the mechanism of awakening very well.

00:09:01.950 --> 00:09:05.590
My own interpretation is that
we're chosen to be regulators...

00:09:05.590 --> 00:09:09.050
to eliminate the inconsistencies
that appear in this world.

00:09:09.190 --> 00:09:14.470
And among those duties is to
fight to regain the real world.

00:09:14.470 --> 00:09:16.730
Still, I wonder about Kaminagi...

00:09:17.900 --> 00:09:19.890
What do you think?

00:09:21.270 --> 00:09:23.740
What? What about her?!

00:09:25.510 --> 00:09:28.480
She may be showing signs of awakening.

00:09:51.500 --> 00:09:53.400
It's no use at all!

00:10:04.650 --> 00:10:07.390
<i>On a morning when she finds</i>
<i>a rainbow-colored shell,</i>

00:10:07.390 --> 00:10:10.220
<i>a girl meets a lone boy on the beach.</i>

00:10:11.820 --> 00:10:15.820
The boy had lost his memory.

00:10:16.830 --> 00:10:19.800
As the two began to
live together in her house,

00:10:19.800 --> 00:10:22.030
they eventually fell in love.
However...

00:10:25.070 --> 00:10:27.800
All of this is just a game.

00:10:34.210 --> 00:10:36.810
So, what's real?

00:10:53.430 --> 00:10:56.960
Tohru Kanou: died in the
first battle to capture Oscar.

00:10:57.470 --> 00:11:00.540
Sachiko Tsumura: suffered massive
data corruption in the same battle.

00:11:00.540 --> 00:11:02.040
Recovery impossible at this time.

00:11:02.040 --> 00:11:05.680
I remember them.
They were both fine soldiers.

00:11:05.680 --> 00:11:09.580
And you still have them
living in Maihama? Why?

00:11:09.680 --> 00:11:12.710
Too many deaths there
would seem unnatural.

00:11:13.320 --> 00:11:16.650
In their case, neither of
them had family to begin with.

00:11:18.820 --> 00:11:21.530
So, you did it to
minimize the effect?

00:11:21.530 --> 00:11:22.960
But, in their case,

00:11:22.960 --> 00:11:28.870
the people around them seemed
not to notice that they were gone.

00:11:29.030 --> 00:11:32.470
Ryoko Kaminagi never
paid such close attention...

00:11:32.470 --> 00:11:35.200
to Tohru Kanou's existence before now.

00:11:35.410 --> 00:11:36.880
Is it possible?

00:11:36.880 --> 00:11:39.210
Did my coming to Maihama affect her?

00:11:39.210 --> 00:11:43.510
Even if it has, perhaps
we should welcome this.

00:11:43.750 --> 00:11:46.550
Just before entering the Maihama server,

00:11:46.550 --> 00:11:49.680
Tohru Kanou caught the
real Maihama on camera.

00:11:50.190 --> 00:11:52.680
It truly was the last day...

00:12:10.380 --> 00:12:12.280
Sorry I'm late!

00:12:15.280 --> 00:12:16.850
Sorry for calling you out of the blue.

00:12:16.850 --> 00:12:19.220
No prob! I was bored, anyway!

00:12:19.220 --> 00:12:20.750
Well, shall we go?

00:12:20.750 --> 00:12:21.980
Hey there!

00:12:23.690 --> 00:12:25.020
Hi!

00:12:25.360 --> 00:12:27.930
Morning! You practice on Sundays, too?

00:12:27.930 --> 00:12:29.590
Yup. Where are you two headed?

00:12:29.900 --> 00:12:32.890
Who cares where we're headed?
Come on, Mizuki!

00:12:35.930 --> 00:12:37.420
See you!

00:12:43.510 --> 00:12:45.570
But why are you scouting locations again?

00:12:45.910 --> 00:12:49.570
It's not just a location hunt.
There's something I want to check out, too.

00:12:49.750 --> 00:12:50.680
What?

00:12:57.960 --> 00:12:59.390
Here.

00:13:09.800 --> 00:13:13.500
What's fake? And what's real?

00:13:46.870 --> 00:13:48.740
What's wrong?

00:13:48.740 --> 00:13:51.170
F-Forget it. It's nothing...

00:13:58.150 --> 00:14:00.310
Sorry for stealing you for the day.

00:14:00.490 --> 00:14:03.080
What's with you? Quit being so formal!

00:14:06.930 --> 00:14:08.720
How long will you stay mad at him?

00:14:09.590 --> 00:14:11.130
You and Sogoru.

00:14:11.130 --> 00:14:13.620
We're not really fighting, just...

00:14:17.840 --> 00:14:21.340
You know I like Hayase, right?

00:14:21.340 --> 00:14:23.570
Yeah, I kinda figured.

00:14:24.210 --> 00:14:26.940
It was a shock to hear
that he had a girlfriend.

00:14:31.350 --> 00:14:35.620
Even so, even if I fail, I'll tell him how
I feel on the night of the festival.

00:14:40.590 --> 00:14:43.060
If I don't, I'll never know for sure.

00:14:47.470 --> 00:14:49.490
You should face your own feelings, Ryoko!

00:14:51.500 --> 00:14:53.100
Mizuki...

00:15:08.920 --> 00:15:12.860
Of course... There are no people.

00:15:22.170 --> 00:15:25.900
This guy is capturing images of the
world deeper than I ever could.

00:15:31.110 --> 00:15:35.480
So what's the point of me
trying to capture images of it?

00:15:38.880 --> 00:15:43.650
The boy was a deserter from
the battlefield of a ruined world.

00:15:44.190 --> 00:15:48.990
But a transmission error
had erased his memories.

00:15:49.430 --> 00:15:52.560
His memories were stored
in the rainbow-colored shell.

00:15:53.600 --> 00:15:57.660
The boy will return
to his world with his friends.

00:15:59.140 --> 00:16:03.770
But if he leaves now, his memories
of this world will be erased.

00:16:04.280 --> 00:16:08.210
So he stores his memories
in the rainbow-colored shell,

00:16:08.210 --> 00:16:11.980
entrusts it to the girl,
and returns to the battlefield.

00:16:36.170 --> 00:16:38.510
All right, and that's it for the first semester.

00:16:38.510 --> 00:16:41.880
Try not to forget too much stuff
over summer break, okay?

00:16:41.880 --> 00:16:43.370
Yes, sir.

00:16:46.890 --> 00:16:50.840
Sogoru! Keep up the good work and
get the swim club up to five members!

00:16:51.190 --> 00:16:52.820
Thanks, sir!

00:16:54.960 --> 00:16:57.060
Finally, summer break!

00:16:57.060 --> 00:16:59.330
Now I can relax a little.

00:16:59.330 --> 00:17:00.490
From what?

00:17:00.730 --> 00:17:04.700
Um, I mean, now I can concentrate
completely on the swim club.

00:17:04.700 --> 00:17:05.760
Oh, I see.

00:17:09.240 --> 00:17:13.180
Now that first semester's over, we can
finally lay down our own burdens, huh?

00:17:13.580 --> 00:17:17.410
Really. Year after year,
we repeat this same ritual.

00:17:21.690 --> 00:17:24.760
Ms. Mizusawa, tonight's the summer festival.

00:17:24.760 --> 00:17:25.590
True.

00:17:39.800 --> 00:17:41.970
Let's get a super ball!

00:17:41.970 --> 00:17:43.210
That's lame!

00:17:43.210 --> 00:17:45.140
Wait up!

00:17:45.240 --> 00:17:48.080
Hayase's sure taking his time.

00:17:48.080 --> 00:17:50.410
Oh! Hayase!

00:17:51.920 --> 00:17:54.380
Hurry up, before all the good spots are taken!

00:17:54.520 --> 00:17:57.780
Okay, everyone's here? Let's go!

00:18:02.030 --> 00:18:04.550
Are you sure about this?
You're not going to go with them?

00:18:07.630 --> 00:18:10.190
Maybe she wants to
avoid any further effects.

00:18:31.120 --> 00:18:32.380
No way...

00:18:34.560 --> 00:18:35.620
Kaminagi?

00:18:36.430 --> 00:18:37.390
What's wrong?

00:18:39.160 --> 00:18:41.760
No... It's nothing.

00:18:50.910 --> 00:18:52.380
Isn't it pretty?

00:18:52.380 --> 00:18:56.110
Yeah. Bad luck, us being
on duty on a night like this.

00:18:56.550 --> 00:18:58.540
Or maybe not such bad luck...

00:18:59.350 --> 00:19:01.440
Nothing.

00:19:41.260 --> 00:19:42.950
We've gotten separated.

00:19:43.060 --> 00:19:44.530
Yeah...

00:19:44.530 --> 00:19:45.790
Oh, well.

00:19:49.630 --> 00:19:51.030
My script...

00:19:52.500 --> 00:19:54.370
I rewrote it.

00:19:59.610 --> 00:20:03.880
The boy who returned to the battlefield
in order to protect this world...

00:20:03.880 --> 00:20:06.410
returned after the war had ended.

00:20:07.350 --> 00:20:10.320
It was now decades in the future.

00:20:11.020 --> 00:20:14.160
There, he found the
rainbow-colored shell...

00:20:14.160 --> 00:20:17.220
which contained
his memories of the girl.

00:20:19.700 --> 00:20:23.690
And then, as he gently
held the shell to his ear...

00:20:24.640 --> 00:20:30.540
he found the shell had broken.
And he heard nothing. Nothing at all.

00:20:34.850 --> 00:20:36.940
Kind of a sad ending, huh?

00:20:37.050 --> 00:20:37.880
Yeah...

00:20:41.890 --> 00:20:43.550
Okay! I'll do it!

00:20:45.320 --> 00:20:47.620
I'm really the only guy for the role, after all!

00:20:48.390 --> 00:20:49.860
Oh, Kyo!

00:20:59.800 --> 00:21:02.300
<i>It's all right. I'm here for you!</i>

00:22:51.580 --> 00:22:54.390
Arque's remaining days alive are running out.

00:22:54.390 --> 00:22:57.820
And yet, why do they both still smile?

00:22:57.820 --> 00:23:01.160
I could never face losing my one, true love.

00:23:01.530 --> 00:23:06.130
Stop it, Chris! Do you think doing
that will make Arque happy?

00:23:06.130 --> 00:23:09.300
I know how hard death is for us,

00:23:09.300 --> 00:23:12.240
but you have to go on living!

00:23:12.840 --> 00:23:15.870
Next time, on Zegapain:
"Lingering Illusions."

00:23:16.340 --> 00:23:18.580
My thoughts, never to be erased.
